For purposes of this division, the following words, terms and phrases, when used in this division, shall have the meanings ascribed to them in this section, except where the context clearly indicates a different meaning:
Candidate: Any individual who has publicly announced candidacy for elected office, filed qualifying documents for elected office, established a campaign committee, accepted campaign contributions, or otherwise meets the definition of "candidate definition of "candidate" under applicable Georgia law.
Campaign activity: Any act intended to advocate for the election or defeat of a candidate, including but not limited to:
(1) Distributing campaign literature, signs, stickers, apparel, or promotional materials for or against a particular candidate(s);
(2) Soliciting votes, endorsements, or campaign contributions for or against a particular candidate(s);
(3) Delivering campaign speeches or statements for or against a particular candidate(s);
(4) Displaying campaign signage, banners, or branded materials for or against a particular candidate(s);
(5) Wearing campaign apparel for promotional purposes for or against a particular candidate(s);
(6) Recording campaign advertisements, videos, livestreams, or social media content for or against a particular candidate(s);
(7) Conducting organized voter outreach or political canvassing for or against a particular candidate(s).
City event: Any event, meeting, ceremony, festival, groundbreaking, ribbon cutting, public celebration, press conference, recreational activity, or other gathering that is:
(1) Organized, sponsored, funded, coordinated, hosted, or substantially supported by the city or a member of the city council; or
(2) Conducted on city-owned property using city personnel, equipment, or financial resources.
City property: Any building, park, street, sidewalk, facility, vehicle, equipment, or real property owned, leased, managed, or controlled by the city.
(Ord. No. 2026-022, § 2, 7-14-2026)

